<item><title>Uganda&apos;s GROW project has lent Shs161 billion to women-owned businesses</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/uganda-s-grow-project-has-lent-shs161-billion-to-women-a171bc/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/uganda-s-grow-project-has-lent-shs161-billion-to-women-a171bc/</guid><category>Uganda</category><description>The World Bank-backed programme has made 10,096 loans, with repayment terms of up to 24 months and interest capped at 10 per cent a year.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:49:01 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" length="32020" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Savanna Fibre targets 1 million more homes across East Africa in 2027</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/savanna-fibre-targets-1-million-more-homes-across-east-9af9d0/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/savanna-fibre-targets-1-million-more-homes-across-east-9af9d0/</guid><category>Uganda</category><description>The rollout follows 250,000 active subscribers in Uganda, Tanzania and Kenya and would take the company&apos;s network past 2 million homes.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:26:32 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" length="32020" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Health Ministry schedules 3.3 million-net drive for Kampala and Wakiso</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/health-ministry-schedules-3-3-million-net-drive-for-kampala-6726af/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/health-ministry-schedules-3-3-million-net-drive-for-kampala-6726af/</guid><category>Uganda</category><description>The three-day distribution, set for November 20 to 22, will send 1,168,700 nets to Kampala and 2,000,216 to Wakiso.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:07:59 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" length="32020" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Kampala traders shut shops to protest URA taxes and enforcement</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/kampala-traders-shut-shops-to-protest-ura-taxes-and-0d0741/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/kampala-traders-shut-shops-to-protest-ura-taxes-and-0d0741/</guid><category>Uganda</category><description>The shutdown closed arcades and commercial buildings as traders called for talks with the Uganda Revenue Authority and a review of business costs.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:27:39 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/kampala-traders-shut-shops-to-protest-ura-taxes-and-0d0741/share.jpg" length="43026" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/kampala-traders-shut-shops-to-protest-ura-taxes-and-0d0741/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Absa Uganda completes Standard Chartered retail and wealth banking acquisition</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/absa-uganda-completes-standard-chartered-retail-and-wealth-5c08fa/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/absa-uganda-completes-standard-chartered-retail-and-wealth-5c08fa/</guid><category>Uganda</category><description>The transfer brings 162 former Standard Chartered employees to Absa, and migrated customers keep their existing products and services.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:37:13 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" length="32020" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
